   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Picture Of You** (1 review): The reviewer identifies this specific track as the highlight of the entire performance [2]\n- **O Is The One That Is Real** (1 other source): This performance marks the first known live rendition of the song [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **At Dawn**: back after 23 archived shows (695 days) [3]\n- **Old Sept Blues**: rare: 14 archived performances [3]\n- **By My Car**: rare: 13 archived performances [3]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: O Is The One That Is Real, Easy Mornin' Rebel [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **mmj2001-12-21.late.flac16** (recommended): soundboard; 12 songs; 78 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]. Said about its sound: The uploader is uncertain if it is soundboard or audience, but notes it is very good [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The lineup likely included KC Guetig on drums, Danny Cash on keys, and JohnnyQ [2]\n- The show occurred the same day the WFPK Xmas Special was recorded [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **mmj2001-12-21.late.flac16**: taped by Dwight R.; transferred by Magnix; source: SBD or AU ? > Tape > Tape [1]. Also: The recording lineage traces from tape to WAV and finally to FLAC level 8 [1]",
